body:
alex: Anyone else hit "crypto.subtle is not a function" when importing the JS SDK from Next.js middleware?

maria: Yep saw that in a customer repro. Edge runtime doesn't provide Node crypto.

kevin: Root cause: one helper in SDK still imports `randomBytes` from node:crypto which then leads to signing code falling back to node APIs. Next Edge has Web Crypto only.

alex: Repro steps I used:
1) create middleware.ts with `import { Redwood } from 'redwood-inference'`
2) deploy to vercel edge
3) request triggers error in logs: `TypeError: crypto.subtle is not a function`

jules: Short-term options:
- provide documentation + sample middleware showing how to lazy-load a tiny shim that binds globalThis.crypto to available webcrypto
- ship an explicit ESM edge export from the SDK that avoids node built-ins

maria: For the shim we recommended to customers, keep it tiny and fail fast so users know their environment lacks Web Crypto rather than getting obscure stack traces. Example snippet for middleware:
```js
// middleware.ts (Next Edge)
export function middleware(req) {
  if (!globalThis.crypto || !globalThis.crypto.subtle) {
    // fail fast during development
    throw new Error('Edge runtime missing Web Crypto APIs. See SDK docs for edge build.');
  }
  // lazy import SDK after verifying crypto
  const { handler } = await import('redwood-inference/edge');
  return handler(req);
}
```

kevin: Implementation plan for SDK: add an `exports` entry `./edge` pointing at `dist/edge/index.mjs` that is built with rollup/tsup and replaces node-specific helpers with WebCrypto implementations. Also emit `index.d.ts` for the edge entry so TS users don't get mismatched types.

alex: TS note: users on Next Edge need `tsconfig` with `lib: ["ES2021", "DOM"]` or `DOM` types otherwise `crypto.subtle` is missing from TS types. Also `module: "esnext"` helps with ESM-only builds.

jules: CI add: small smoke job that runs a tiny Next Edge handler in `@vercel/edge-runtime` or `miniflare` to catch regressions. Failing that, at least run a Node-free lint that checks for `require('crypto')` or `import crypto` in the SDK source paths intended for edge.

sdk-bot: Issue created #1377 "edge: add ESM-only WebCrypto build + Next middleware docs" assigned to @kevin and @jules.

alex: I'll add the shim + a short troubleshooting blurb to the getting-started Next sample app and onboarding checklist so customers see it early.

maria: Also add a one-liner in README: "Edge runtimes (Next.js middleware) do not include Node built-ins; use the SDK edge export or ensure Web Crypto is available."

kevin: I'll draft the build config and push a PR that adds `dist/edge` artifacts, types, and the exports map. If anyone has edge-specific unit tests, drop them in `test/edge-smoke/`.

jules: Nice. That should reduce onboarding friction and cut down support noise. :+1:

alex: Thanks team — closing for now, will follow up when PR is up.
